+ * LINUX64 (xnulinux): the first return of a new user thread (thread_bootstrap_return) while hosted. The pending ASTs
+ * run as on the way to user space (for the first BSD thread: bsdinit_task, which execs launchd), and the thread enters
+ * user space through linux64_el0_run (the host is told where user space starts the first time).
